# Build outputs
system/prisc+x
system/chtpm_parser_pal
system/keyboard_input
system/renderer
ops/+x/

# The same four on win32. MSYS2 MinGW appends .exe, so the extensionless
# patterns above match NOTHING on Windows and every build left three untracked
# binaries in the tree. ops/+x/ was already covered because it ignores the
# whole directory. Keeping both forms here is the difference between a
# one-command rebuild and an untracked-artifact mess.
system/prisc+x.exe
system/chtpm_parser_pal.exe
system/keyboard_input.exe
system/renderer.exe

# Runtime state - never commit. The whole pieces/ tree is written by the
# running harness (key histories, the rendered frame, gui_state, the
# cursor files), and chats/ holds the user's own conversation history.
pieces/
chats/

# Dropped by chtpm_parser_pal's ${var} substitution debug path while
# rendering. Runtime noise.
text_substitution_debug.txt
debug.txt

# House standard: ignore editor and OS droppings.
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# NOTE on the binaries above: this house generally commits built +x
# artifacts, but these are all one-command rebuilds from scripts/build.sh
# and they are architecture-specific, so they are kept out of history.
# Flip that by removing the block above if the house convention is
# confirmed to be "commit the binaries".